  "content": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gate behaviour across the full growth curve"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockquote",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Directive — Test the charter criterion that mid-exponential performance is retained into stationary phase."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Every 20 minutes from lag through 2 hours into stationary. Same eight input states as entry 12."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The single measurement most circuit papers omit, and the one the charter singled out: a gate characterised only at mid-exponential is characterised in its best conditions."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Result"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "26-fold at mid-exponential falls to 17-fold at stationary onset — 65 percent retained, just above the 60 percent criterion."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The loss is asymmetric: the OFF state rises while the ON state is roughly flat, consistent with reduced repressor turnover rather than with reporter accumulation."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Interpretation"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Criterion met, but with little margin. Any change that raises the OFF state — including the entry-06 read-through, if a future build abandons divergent orientation — would push this below criterion."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
